# No filename here carries a content hash, so nothing can be cached
# indefinitely without risking a stale asset after the next deploy — this
# site ships several times a day. HTML always revalidates: it's what changes
# most and must never be served stale. CSS/JS/JSON get a short cache so a
# repeat visit within the same session skips the revalidation round trip
# without risking more than an hour of staleness. Images and favicons change
# rarely, so they get a longer window — still bounded, still must-revalidate.

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate

/*.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate

/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, must-revalidate

/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, must-revalidate

/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, must-revalidate

/*.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, must-revalidate
